### 1. My Path To Writing in IDE
@1-path-to-ide

Personal journey from skepticism to adopting Trae IDE for non-coding work. Motivation, prior experience, subscription trigger, and discovery that IDE-driven writing improved readability and changed the author’s writing approach versus chatbot-only workflows.

### 2. Example AI-Powered Writing Workflow
@2-workflow

High-level human–AI division of labor: humans focus on creative thinking and validation; AI assists with technical, structured steps. Presents the step-by-step workflow used for long-form pieces.

#### Step 1. Brain-dumping

Create a folder and `braindump.mkd`. Dictate or write ideas (any language), lightly structure with Markdown, optionally add `<TBD>` tags to mark gaps.

#### Step 2. Creating an Outline
Generate `outline.mkd` from the braindump via the IDE agent; then manually refine the outline. Include `@` lines to define section file names and order.

#### Step 3. Generating section files

Use IDE prompts with `outline_rules` and `article_rules` to auto-create section files. Prefer multiple files over a single long draft for quality, focus, and easier targeted edits.

#### Step 4. Expanding and Validating

Expand AI-generated sections where needed, adding missing micro-ideas. Choose manual writing or guided AI expansion; preserve short versions before large edits when useful.

#### Step 5. Committing Before AI Changes

Commit work-in-progress to Git to snapshot the baseline. Use concise conventional commit messages and push when appropriate to track upcoming AI edits.

#### Step 6. AI-Driven Refining / Polishing

Enhance selected files according to `article_rules`. Review diffs side-by-side, accept or reject changes paragraph by paragraph, and restore originals when the AI over-edits.

### Final steps
@3-final-steps

Combine section files into one Markdown via a simple script. Paste into Google Docs using “Paste from Markdown”, then manually insert images and finalize formatting for publication.

### The Best AI IDE Features
@4-best-features

Key advantages: diff-based review of AI edits and reuse of instructions and prior pieces as style/context. Notes on when autocompletion helps (and when it doesn’t) for creative writing.

### Conclusion
@conclusion

AI IDEs enable a practical, repeatable workflow for long-form writing: they streamline technical steps while preserving author creativity, resulting in clearer, faster, and more consistent posts.